1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,858
On a Sunday night, Sam texted Dana asking for the usual: brand voice notes, so he

2
00:00:04,858 --> 00:00:06,583
could start briefing the batch.

3
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:08,141
Dana didn't send tone words.

4
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:12,648
She sent her price, her margin, and the one claim she will not let an ad make, no

5
00:00:12,648 --> 00:00:14,040
matter how well it tests.

6
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:17,601
That's the whole design of this section, stated as one exchange.

7
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:21,831
Section one gave you a number: around twenty variants to find a real winner.

8
00:00:21,831 --> 00:00:26,283
This section makes sure those twenty are actually twenty different bets, not one

9
00:00:26,283 --> 00:00:27,841
idea wearing twenty outfits.

10
00:00:27,841 --> 00:00:30,567
Everything here happens before a generator opens.

11
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:35,242
The product truth, the awareness levels, the hooks, the angle map, the landing page:

12
00:00:35,242 --> 00:00:36,355
it all has to match.

13
00:00:36,355 --> 00:00:38,859
Skip this section and generation still works.

14
00:00:38,859 --> 00:00:42,755
It just produces twenty confident variations of the same narrow guess.

15
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:47,342
Five pieces, building toward the workshop where you write a real brief.

16
00:00:47,342 --> 00:00:51,948
Product truth comes first, because every claim your ads make has to trace back to

17
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:54,507
something true and something Dana can defend.

18
00:00:54,507 --> 00:00:59,284
Awareness levels and the hook taxonomy give you the actual vocabulary for a testable

19
00:00:59,284 --> 00:01:04,061
angle, instead of "make it punchier." The angle map turns all of it into twenty real

20
00:01:04,061 --> 00:01:04,345
bets.

21
00:01:04,345 --> 00:01:08,951
And landing congruence closes the loop: the best hook in the world still loses if

22
00:01:08,951 --> 00:01:11,908
the page it lands on breaks the promise the ad made.

23
00:01:11,908 --> 00:01:14,353
Before the next lecture, open a blank note.

24
00:01:14,353 --> 00:01:19,016
Write down your own price, what it actually costs you to deliver, and the one line

25
00:01:19,016 --> 00:01:22,883
about your product you would not want to defend under bright lights.

26
00:01:22,883 --> 00:01:27,546
That's the first three lines of your own product truth document, and it is exactly

27
00:01:27,546 --> 00:01:30,333
what the workshop in 2.6 turns into artifact B01.
